  "title": "Origins of the caliphate",
  "summary": "After Muhammad died in 632 CE, Abu Bakr became the first caliph, with Umar ibn al-Khattab backing him. Sunnis say the caliph should be chosen by the community, while Shi'a hold that God appointed Ali, and the dispute produced a major split in Islam. Abu Bakr then fought tribes that left Islam or withheld the alms tax, reuniting Arabia.",
